            include this policy's own wording quoted inside a commit message, a search for the flag
            name in a file, and a git subcommand the policy does not cover. Each is a shape a
            substring matcher refuses and git would have run, and a guard whose first act is to
            break a working session trains its owner to disable it. The false positive surface is
            therefore part of the design rather than an afterthought, which is why the token stream
            is parsed and the flag recognised only where git would recognise it.},
  check  = {cmd:.venv/bin/python3 -m pytest tests/test_no_verify.py -k test_ordinary_commands_are_not_refused},
}

@misc{hooks-no-verify-an-unparseable-command-is-not-a-bypass,
