            about a wrapper reporting itself, and between them it read bazel's exit code as the
            target's health. It refused a correct commit on that reading: six targets were reported
            red before the probe while bazel printed a passing test tally and its own success line.
            Bazel had exited thirty-eight because its build event upload failed, the telemetry
            Service having been deleted after the node hit disk pressure and evicted fifty-seven
            pods. The sink was gone and the tests were green. The behaviour was reproduced
            deliberately rather than inferred, by pointing the build event backend at a closed port
            over a passing target. The first repair was wrong in the direction that hides defects:
            it asked whether a failure line was present and treated its absence as green, and the
            second arm refuted it in one run, because a request for a nonexistent target exits
            nonzero and prints an error carrying none of the failure markers, so a missing target
            read as clean. The predicate is therefore positive rather than negative: bazel must
            state its own success and print a test tally, and anything else with a nonzero status is
            reported as unexplained rather than absorbed into either verdict. It is deliberately not
            keyed on the specific exit code, because keying on the number would make the next
            infrastructure code a false red, and this witness can no more enumerate bazel's exit
            codes than an arm here could enumerate a census's declared state vocabulary.},
  check  = {cmd:.venv/bin/python3 -m pytest tests/test_bar_fires.py -k test_the_witness_reads_bazels_artifact_not_its_exit_status},
}

@misc{hooks-bar-fires-no-conventional-under-declaration-survives,
  section = {bar-fires},
  title  = {A shared habit is the only omission that collides},
  claim  = {The operator ruled that there is no false green risk if cache keys are constructed
            properly, and that if they are not constructed properly the risk does not depend on
            peers to cause the collision, so a builder collides with its own earlier entry and
            cache sharing is not the variable. That locates the residual risk precisely, because
            poisoning requires both parties' keys to be improper in the same way: an under-declaring
            producer computes a key describing the narrower action it actually performed, and a
            consumer receives that entry only by making the identical omission. Idiosyncratic
            sloppiness is therefore harmless, since it produces keys nobody else computes, and a
            shared habit across repositories is the only thing that can collide. The conventional
            candidates are undeclared host tools, reads of the home directory, and a path call that
            follows runfiles symlinks back out to the working tree. All three measure clean here.
            The first probe written to audit them was blind in exactly the way it was auditing for:
            it reported three instances of the escaping path call and all three were comments
            explaining why not to write one, which is the rule this ecosystem records about a corpus
            containing prose about itself. Re-measured through the syntax tree rather than the text,
            the count is zero, with a control confirming the reader finds calls of that method at
            all. The host-tool arm had the same shape, appearing to show a document converter
            invoked from a distribution that does not declare it, where reading the sites showed two
            comments and one test fixture string.},
  check  = {cmd:.venv/bin/python3 -m pytest tests/test_bar_fires.py -k test_no_conventional_under_declaration_survives_in_this_tree},
}

@misc{hooks-bar-fires-every-warrant-check-resolves,
  section = {bar-fires},
  claim   = {Counting is a different predicate from resolving, and fifty-five checks accumulated in
            the gap between them. This distribution's warrants are one-to-one with its test
            functions and the gate verifies that ratio on every commit, yet fifty-five claims
            carried a check naming a runner that does not exist: the project file declares exactly
            one runner, addressed by a prefix, and those checks omitted it. All fifty-five were
            written by one session at one per tick, each beside a real arm that passes, so the arm
            was sound and the address was unresolvable. Nothing in this tree could detect it,
            because no tool here parses a check field; the tool that would is the projection engine
            and it is not installed. The warrant-to-test ratio was therefore verified continuously
            while the checks' executability was never verified at all. The mechanism was accepted
            into a fleet census as wider than the four that census listed, since those all assume
            the check resolves and asks the wrong question, where this is the case in which
            resolution never happens and no arm notices. This arm resolves rather than counts: for
            every check it parses the module named and requires the named function to be defined
            there, with a floor on how many checks it parsed so that a reader reading the wrong
            shape cannot report zero failures vacuously.},
  check   = {cmd:.venv/bin/python3 -m pytest tests/test_bar_fires.py -k test_every_warrant_check_resolves_to_a_test_that_exists}
}

@misc{hooks-bar-fires-census-this-repo-hosts-declares-vocabulary,
  section = {bar-fires},
  title   = {A census this repo HOSTS declares the vocabulary its own §S uses},
  note    = {The poll read `8 filed + 0 pending` over a CENSUS-vfs §S in which three parties had
            filed and five had not. The count was arithmetically perfect over the wrong population:
            every row carried the mark `filed elsewhere`, but five of them read `filed elsewhere
            when it files`, which names a DESTINATION rather than a state — where a leg would go,
            not that one exists. The distinction had already been argued in that section's own
            prose two paragraphs above the table, and the table then fused both halves into the one
            phrase the reader matches, so a stated distinction that the vocabulary does not encode
            had not in fact been made. A `state | means` table is what makes such a split
            machine-readable, and this census published none, which the poll reported honestly as a
            fact about its reader while the defect was in the document and only its host could
            repair it. The arm is keyed on the predicate rather than on a filename: the population
            is every census whose roster marks this repo as hosting the file, so a census hosted
            later is covered on the day it is created and the population cannot itself become the
            mis-named one. It carries two controls. The population is asserted non-empty, since the
            marking phrase is one a future edit could reword and an empty population would pass the
            arm vacuously. The reader's exit status is asserted zero per file, because a reader
            that did not run cannot report an absence. On its first run it measured one of two
            hosted censuses undeclared, the second supplying a positive control from the same
            reader over the same corpus, and it also surfaced that the row describing the host was
            itself stale — it read `when it files` two commits after the host had filed.},
  check   = {cmd:.venv/bin/python3 -m pytest tests/test_bar_fires.py -k test_a_census_this_repo_hosts_declares_the_vocabulary_its_own_status_uses}
}

@misc{hooks-bar-fires-classifier-count-printed-not-merely-computed,
  section = {bar-fires},
  title   = {The classifier's count is printed, not merely computed},
  note    = {The poll computed the document-relative classification for every census whose status
            table it could find — each row read against the states that census itself declares, by
            the mode built for exactly that — assigned it to a variable, and never printed it. Only
            a conditional pointer telling a reader to re-run the tool by hand was ever emitted, so
            what a reader actually saw was four hand-written prefix terms. That is the defect the
            surrounding comment names one level in: the block argues at length that shipping a
            classifier and not consuming it is the packager failing to use its own package, adds
            the wiring, and then discards the wired value before the report. A computed value
            nothing prints is a caller that does not consume its own call. It is also the half that
            rescues the partition, because the four terms are one query run with four different
            prefixes: when the prefixes match nothing, all four read zero, their total reads zero,
            and they agree with each other because they are one failure counted four times.
            Printing the operands cannot detect that, since the rule it satisfies is about hidden
            operands rather than shared sources; only a term drawn from a different measurement
            can. Measured at the tick this landed, on three censuses at once: two of them printed a
            four-term partition of all zeros over status tables of eight and twelve rows while the
            documents' own vocabularies named eight of eight and eleven of twelve, which localises
            one genuinely undeclared row and separates it from twelve reader failures that had been
            indistinguishable from it. The hand-written prefixes are kept rather than replaced,
            because three censuses publish no vocabulary at all and the classifier refuses those
            while the prefixes still say something; the two readings answer different questions and
            the poll prints both rather than reconciling them, since reconciling them in the script
            would be judgement in the turn rather than a measurement a reader can check. Where no
            vocabulary is published the line reports a refusal rather than a zero, because a count
            of zero and a reading that could not be made are different facts and only one of them
            is about the census. The arm asserts both that the value is still computed, so it
            cannot pass by the classifier call being deleted, and that the value reaches an echo,
            which is the only interface this script has.},
  check   = {cmd:.venv/bin/python3 -m pytest tests/test_bar_fires.py -k test_the_classifiers_count_is_printed_and_not_merely_computed}
}

@misc{hooks-bar-fires-second-source-not-gated-on-divergence,
  section = {bar-fires},
  title   = {The second source is not gated on the divergence branch},
  note    = {A sibling arm exists because the document-relative reading once sat inside the branch
            that fires only when the status table and HEAD disagree, so a census whose totals agree
            printed neither a reading nor a refusal. That was repaired by hoisting the line out of
            the branch. One tick later the second-source count was added back INSIDE that same
            branch, reproducing the defect the sibling arm was written to prevent, in the script it
            was written about. Measured: two censuses agree on totals, so the block was skipped and
            neither printed the line, while the four that did print one were exactly the four that
            diverge — which reads as a property of those censuses and is a property of the branch.
            The cause was also misdiagnosed twice. The carried symbol said the status-table finder
            does not match a three-column party-status-evidence header; run against the finder's own
            predicate that header matches, so the finder was never why the census was silent, and
            the sibling arm's own docstring already records that identical misdiagnosis from the
            tick before. The repair removed rather than moved the gated emission, because the two
            computations were the same classify call on the same table: two readings of one source
            are not two sources, and keeping both would suggest corroboration the poll does not
            have. The second-source framing moved down to the ungated line, and the no-vocabulary
            path now states that the prefix terms are then the only reading and share one source,
            since a refusal that does not say what remains leaves four agreeing zeros looking
            corroborated. The assertion is structural rather than textual, because requiring the
            string to appear somewhere is exactly what let the regression through: the previous arm
            required the value to reach an echo and it did, an unreachable one. Two further reader
            defects were found while writing it and are guarded here — the emission is located by
            its text rather than by a line starting with the verb, since this poll wraps echoes
            with a backslash so the reported string sits on the following line, and comment lines
            are excluded so the arm cannot pass on a comment that merely mentions the phrase.},
  check   = {cmd:.venv/bin/python3 -m pytest tests/test_bar_fires.py -k test_the_second_source_is_not_gated_on_the_divergence_branch}
}

@misc{hooks-bar-fires-gap-verdict-uses-declared-vocabulary,
  section = {bar-fires},
  title   = {The gap verdict uses the declared vocabulary when the prefixes cannot},
  note    = {Two censuses reached no verdict at all while their own vocabularies answered
            perfectly. Both printed a four-term partition of zeros over status tables of eight and
            twelve rows, so the arm took its refusal branch and correctly declined to call the
            zeros a finding — while three lines below, the document-relative reading partitioned
            the same rows without residue, one of them into three filed and five not-yet-filed
            against a roster of eight. The four prefixes were the last hand-written population in
            this poll, and their provenance is the defect: they were written from the two censuses
            their author happened to be reading at the time. This session then rewrote one of those
            censuses' status sections to use a different pair of states, and the prefixes matched
            none of it — a hand-written vocabulary made stale by its own author's edit, inside the
            arm built to catch stale hand-written vocabularies. What the verdict needs is a count of
            rows carrying a state that explains an absent leg, and the classifier already produces
            exactly that from the census's own declarations, so a census whose vocabulary partitions
            its status table can be adjudicated rather than refused. The refusal branch survives and
            the arm requires it to, because three censuses publish no vocabulary at all and the
            classifier refuses those while the prefixes still say something; a repair that
            adjudicated every census by deleting the refusal would trade a blind spot for a false
            verdict. The report names which instrument produced the figure, because a verdict that
            silently switched sources would print two different measurements under one label, which
            is the manufactured corroboration this poll refuses elsewhere. Measured after: the two
            censuses reach a verdict labelled by declared states, the three the prefixes could
            already adjudicate print the unchanged plain verdict, and none falls into the refusal.},
  check   = {cmd:.venv/bin/python3 -m pytest tests/test_bar_fires.py -k test_the_gap_verdict_uses_the_declared_vocabulary_when_the_prefixes_cannot}
}

@misc{hooks-bar-fires-every-census-declares-every-state-it-uses,
  section = {bar-fires},
  title   = {Every census declares every state its own status rows use},
  note    = {Two frozen censuses each carried one status row using a state their own vocabulary
            never declared, and both rows were right. One read that a party had filed elsewhere at
            a given revision, against a vocabulary declaring only filed-at-revision, which its own
            entry defines as present in THIS repository's HEAD and verified there; that party's leg
            is in that party's own tree, so the row is accurate and the state is real. The other
            read that a party's leg was written and untracked, and that cell says outright which
            declared state it is not — its author knew none fitted and wrote the negation into the
            row rather than choosing a wrong state. Neither is a defect in a row. Both are the
            vocabulary being narrower than the fleet's actual states: a domain each census
            partitioned correctly until a case arrived that it could not express. Filed and filed
            elsewhere were one cell until a leg landed in another party's tree; filed and written
            but untracked were one cell until a leg existed on disk and in no commit anywhere. The
            prefix rule is why neither falls back to the shorter state: a declared state that
            continues with a further word is treated as ambiguous rather than as a match, and that
            refusal is correct, since silently reading the longer state as the shorter one would
            report a leg in another tree as a leg in this one. The rows are untouched by operator
            ruling, which permitted the vocabulary alone to be amended after the freeze; the
            resulting diff is one insertion per census with no deletion and no modification, so no
            filing status moved and no accounting changed. The arm scopes its read to the status
            table rather than the whole document, because a peer measured that the classifier walks
            every table and an unscoped read counts revision-log and roster rows as residue. It
            treats the reader's refusal on a census publishing no vocabulary as a refusal rather
            than as residue, since counting those would report the reader instead of the corpus,
            and it asserts that at least one census was readable so an all-refused run cannot pass
            as a clean one.},
  check   = {cmd:.venv/bin/python3 -m pytest tests/test_bar_fires.py -k test_every_census_declares_every_state_its_own_status_rows_use}
}

@misc{hooks-bar-fires-gate-refuses-a-new-ragged-row,
  section = {bar-fires},
  title   = {The gate refuses a ragged row it did not already have},
  note    = {A peer's line-based arm has been finding ragged table rows in this repository from
            outside it, and they measured why that is not enough: their arm fires at their own
            commit on their own repository, so a peer file is swept strictly later than the write
            and often later than someone else's repair. Every party in this fleet writes rows into
            every other party's censuses, so every structural arm in the fleet has the same hole,
            and the gate that runs when the bytes land is the receiver's. That is the one moment a
            write and a check coincide. The defect is also unreadable to every reader here that
            goes through the parse, since a short row is padded to its header's width before the
            AST exists, so the rule lives in the line-based shape linter and the gate reads it
            there. It is armed against new rows only, and that difference is the whole design: a
            first sweep measured fifteen ragged rows across thirteen files, several in frozen
            censuses and two in this session's own filed legs, none of which may be amended under
            standing constraints. Arming a gate over a tree that does not pass it blocks the
            commits that would clean it, which this corpus records as a measured hazard, so the
            refusal reads the same path out of HEAD and fires only on an increase. The comparison
            is a count rather than a set of lines, and the weakness is stated rather than hidden:
            moving a ragged row while adding another elsewhere holds the count and passes. Set
            membership is the stronger form and belongs with the ratchet's machinery; a count
            catches the case this gate exists for, which is a row that was not ragged becoming
            ragged. The linter's output is captured to a file rather than piped into a counter,
            because the linter exits nonzero when it has findings and a pipe would report the
            counter's status instead, turning a crashed reader into a clean document — a false
            zero from the instrument, inside the check built to catch false reads; the gate
            separates a linter that could not run from a document with no findings and says which.
            The arm asserts the property rather than a spelling, after a first cut named a literal
            command string that the gate writes differently — an arm that names a spelling cannot
            outlive a rename, which this file has now measured three times on one comparison arm.},
  check   = {cmd:.venv/bin/python3 -m pytest tests/test_bar_fires.py -k test_the_gate_refuses_a_ragged_row_it_did_not_already_have}
}

@misc{hooks-bar-fires-refusal-record-ragged-rows-by-shape,
  section = {bar-fires},
  title   = {The refusal record's ragged rows are reported by shape},
  note    = {The poll printed a count of ragged rows in the refusal record followed by one
            sentence naming their cause, and an earlier tick had already corrected the COUNT after
            it was carried from memory as two when a field count found three. The count has been
            right ever since; the sentence attached to it was not. Measured by reading the rows
            rather than counting them, the three are two shapes: rows with three fields carry
            neither a session id nor a gate name and are genuinely pre-schema, while a row with
            four fields carries a session id and lacks only the gate name. So the phrase calling
            them unattributable is true of the first shape and false of the second — that row IS
            attributable to a session, and its actual gap is which gate refused. A reader acting
            on the collapsed sentence looks for a missing attribution that is present and misses
            the one that is absent. That is a correct count under a mis-named cause, arriving one
            layer down from the correct count this same figure produced when its numerator was
            wrong. The line also now names its subject: the record lives in a host-local cache
            rather than in the repository, so no commit can move it, which is why the numerator sat
            static across many ticks while being re-derived as a carried blocker each time. A
            reader watching it for movement was watching an artifact this repository does not
            write. The arm checks the poll's shape rather than the record's content, because the
            record is host-local and may legitimately be absent or hold different rows elsewhere;
            what must hold is that the two shapes are counted apart rather than collapsed. It
            carries a positive control requiring the record to still be read at all, so the
            assertions cannot pass by the section vanishing.},
  check   = {cmd:.venv/bin/python3 -m pytest tests/test_bar_fires.py -k test_the_refusal_records_ragged_rows_are_reported_by_shape}
}

@misc{hooks-bar-fires-poll-does-not-re-ask-an-answered-question,
  section = {bar-fires},
  title   = {The poll does not re-ask a question it has already answered},
  note    = {The poll exceeded a foreground time limit on every tick for several ticks, and every
            time the response was that a duration is not a property, followed by backgrounding it.
            That is true about seconds and useless as a diagnosis. The property is how many times
            the reader process is STARTED, which does not change when an unrelated job runs, and it
            was measurable throughout. Measured from the source, because neither alternative was
            admissible: a shim placed on the search path cannot intercept the calls, since the poll
            resolves the reader by an absolute path; and swapping the real binary for a counting
            one would work but is refused, because eight peer sessions run in this shared tree and
            a swapped binary is precisely the concurrency hazard measured one tick earlier, when
            another party's planted defect was captured by this session's own build and reported as
            a failure in a distribution it had not touched. Twenty-two invocation sites sit inside
            the per-census loop and two outside it; against ten censuses that is two hundred and
            twenty-two process starts for one run. The actionable half is not the total: one reader
            mode is invoked eleven times on the same file within a single iteration and another
            nine, which is the identical query against an unchanged path, whose answer cannot
            differ between calls. Roughly two hundred of those starts re-ask something already
            answered. The arm therefore bounds the per-mode repeat count rather than the total,
            because a total would fall when a census is deleted and rise when one is added,
            reporting the corpus instead of the poll, while the repeat count is a property of the
            script alone and moves only when someone adds another redundant call. The ceiling is
            the instrument's own measurement rather than a round number chosen for comfort, so any
            rise is a change someone made rather than a threshold crossed. The loop header is read
            from the source rather than assumed, after a first attempt searched for a spelling the
            script does not use, and the arm asserts that some reader call was found so that an
            empty result cannot read as an absence of repeats.},
  check   = {cmd:.venv/bin/python3 -m pytest tests/test_bar_fires.py -k test_the_poll_does_not_re_ask_a_question_it_has_already_answered}
}

@misc{hooks-bar-fires-poll-states-no-underivable-paydown-figure,
  section = {bar-fires},
  title   = {The poll states no paydown figure it cannot re-derive},
  note    = {The poll announced a blocked paydown as a three-part sum with a total, typed into the
            script, and reprinted it unchanged every run. Measured two ticks after a paydown moved
            one of the terms, that term was three lower than stated and another had GROWN by two
            from suppression directives added during the same work, so the figure was wrong in both
            directions at once. This is the defect the poll exists to prevent, occurring inside the
            poll: its own opening states that a claim with no re-derivation procedure will not be
            re-checked however load-bearing it is, because nothing about it announces that it could
            be, and a typed count announces nothing. The placement made it worse, since the figure
            sat in the section reporting carried operator decisions — precisely the number a reader
            consults to judge whether a decision is still worth its cost. It was also the partition
            shape this corpus refuses elsewhere: three terms and a total originating in one act of
            typing, agreeing with each other because they were written together, which is agreement
            carrying no information. The repair deliberately does not derive the figure in the
            poll. Three checker runs per invocation would add three process starts to a script
            measured at two hundred and twenty-two, and the honest alternative to a stale number is
            no number together with the command that yields a fresh one, which a reader can run
            when the size actually matters. The arm matches the SHAPE — a bare count adjacent to a
            distribution name — rather than the particular digits, because updating the numbers by
            hand is the move that produced the defect and would otherwise satisfy the check. It
            carries a positive control requiring the decision itself to still be reported, so the
            assertion cannot pass by the section disappearing.},
  check   = {cmd:.venv/bin/python3 -m pytest tests/test_bar_fires.py -k test_the_poll_states_no_paydown_figure_it_cannot_re_derive}
}
