  note    = {The first version of this arm was vacuous and its falsification arm is what said so.
            It asserted that a dash-leading path behind a terminator refuses, which passes with
            the terminator disabled, because the suffix test alone already keeps that token out of
            the option pile: the arm named the terminator and measured something else. The case
            that discriminates is in the pattern-dropping branch, where the search program drops
            its first bare word as the pattern, so a claimed path that is the only bare word is
            eaten unless the terminator routes it past that loop. Measured both ways, the verdict
            flips with the terminator planted off. The control beside it pins that a lone bare word
            with no terminator is still read as a pattern, because refusing that would be a false
            positive and is what separates this fix from a broader refusal. The terminator changes
            the MEANING of a token rather than its shape, so the gate follows the caller's
            declaration instead of guessing.},
  check   = {cmd:.venv/bin/python3 -m pytest tests/test_structural_query.py -k test_an_operand_after_a_terminator_escapes_the_pattern_drop}
}

